  "id": "Compound::DB00754 - Gene::6335",
  "verbalization": "Ethotoin appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving the Scn9a subunit. The evidence suggests that Ethotoin binds to multiple sodium channel subunits—Scn7a, Scn11a, and Scn8a—each of which participates in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This interaction is further supported by the fact that all three subunits are ultimately involved in the activity of Scn9a. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Ethotoin and the involvement of Scn9a in sodium channel function. The overlapping pathways suggest that Ethotoin may modulate sodium channel activity through a common mechanism, potentially affecting Scn9a in a general way. The integration of these findings implies that Ethotoin could influence sodium channel function by targeting multiple subunits, which in turn may affect Scn9a’s role in cellular electrical signaling.",
